course: dictionary
lesson: 6849
title: The word outsider
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An outsider is someone who is not part of a group, or who is not accepted by it. Context tells you which meaning fits. «Maya felt like an outsider on her first day at the new school, because everyone already knew each other.» Maya is not in the group yet, so outsider means someone who does not belong.
explain: The same word can mean someone from another place or organisation. «Lines drawn by outsiders cut through peoples, farms and families.» Here outsiders are people from somewhere else, who were not part of those communities. Ask yourself: is this person outside the group, or from outside the place?
explain: In sport, an outsider is a team, person or horse that is not expected to win. «The outsider won the race!» Nobody thought it would win, so the surprise is the clue. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "The team nobody expected to win won the race" still makes sense.
fact: An outsider is a person who does not belong to a group, or is not accepted by it.
fact: An outsider can also be someone from another place or organisation, not part of it.
fact: In sport, an outsider is a person, team or horse that is not expected to win.
fact: «Lǎowài» (LAOW-WIGH) is a casual word for foreigner, literally "old outsider"; many people use it without harm, but some dislike the label.
fact: Cahokia, by the Mississippi, was about as big as London around 1100, but outsiders forgot it.
exercise: «Maya felt like an outsider on her first day at the new school.» What does outsider mean here? | *Someone who does not belong to the group yet | A pupil who is always first in the line | A teacher who gives out the homework
exercise: «The outsider won the race!» What is an outsider in a race? | The person who cheers loudest at the finish | A race that is never finished | *A horse or runner nobody expected to win
exercise: «Lǎowài» is a casual word for what? | A shopkeeper | A grandparent | *A foreigner
test: Which sentence uses outsider to mean a person from another place? | *«Lines drawn by outsiders cut through peoples, farms and families.» | «The outsider won the race!» | «Maya felt like an outsider at her new school.»
test: Which meaning fits «The outsider won the race!»? | A person who is not accepted by a group | *A team or horse nobody expected to win | A stranger from another country
exam: Using the clues, what does outsider mean in «Cahokia was a big city that outsiders forgot»? | Animals that live outdoors | People who know the city very well | A type of wooden house | *People from outside the place, who had never been there
